  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between Pongachalconel and Potassium voltage-gated channel subfamily KQT member 4, with Neuraminidase acting as a common target in all three paths. Each of the three pathways links Pongachalconel to Neuraminidase, which is then targeted by different compounds—3,7,3',4'-Tetrahydroxyflavanone, Acetaminophen Glucuronide, and Spirolide H—all of which ultimately target the same potassium channel. This indicates that Pongachalconel may exert its effects through a shared mechanism that indirectly influences Neuraminidase, which in turn interacts with the potassium channel. The consistent targeting of the potassium channel across these pathways suggests a potential role in the biological response to Pongachalconel, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Pongachalconel may modulate Neuraminidase activity, which could then influence the potassium channel, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this link.",
